</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Native transport implementations.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Adapter interfaces. ‣ 4.2 Transport Adapters ‣ 4 Protocol Specification and Implementation ‣ AWCP: A Workspace Delegation Protocol for Deep-Engagement Collaboration across Remote Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> compares the four transport adapters along key operational dimensions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SSHFS</span> transport projects the Delegator’s workspace via a FUSE-based mount <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> over an SSH tunnel with ephemeral credentials, providing bidirectional real-time synchronization ideal for interactive tasks.
The <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Archive</span> transport serializes the workspace into a base64-encoded ZIP archive transmitted inline within the <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">START</span> message, offering a self-contained mechanism that requires no external infrastructure.
The <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Storage</span> transport decouples data transfer from the control channel via pre-signed URLs, accommodating cloud-native deployments where large workspaces can be exchanged through object storage services.
The <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Git</span> transport leverages branch-based version control, with each snapshot corresponding to a commit that provides a full audit trail of workspace modifications.
As discussed in §<a href="#S2" title="2 Related Work ‣ AWCP: A Workspace Delegation Protocol for Deep-Engagement Collaboration across Remote Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, recent Git-based coordination systems <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite> independently validate this design; AWCP’s adapter generalizes the pattern into a transport-agnostic component of the delegation lifecycle.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Snapshot reconciliation.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For transports that do not support live synchronization, the Executor periodically captures workspace snapshots, which are compressed archives of the current file state, and subsequently transmits them to the Delegator via SSE events.
The Delegator processes these snapshots according to a configurable <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">snapshot policy</span> with three modes: <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">auto</span>, which applies incoming snapshots immediately; <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">staged</span>, which queues snapshots for explicit approval by the Delegator agent or a human operator; and <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">discard</span>, which ignores snapshots entirely for read-only delegations.
When a transport reports live synchronization capability, the policy is overridden to <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">auto</span>, as the mounted filesystem already reflects the latest state.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Engineering Overview</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The reference implementation is structured as an npm workspace monorepo comprising eight packages organized by the dependency hierarchy shown in Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.3 Engineering Overview ‣ 4 Protocol Specification and Implementation ‣ AWCP: A Workspace Delegation Protocol for Deep-Engagement Collaboration across Remote Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
The <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@awcp/core</span> package contains the protocol types, dual state machines, and error definitions with zero external dependencies, ensuring that the protocol specification remains portable.
The <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@awcp/sdk</span> builds upon the core package to provide the <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">DelegatorService</span> and <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ExecutorService</span> with JSON-based state persistence, enabling crash recovery across sessions.
The four transport packages each export a <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">DelegatorTransport</span> and <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ExecutorTransport</span> pair conforming to the adapter interfaces described in §<a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Transport Adapters ‣ 4 Protocol Specification and Implementation ‣ AWCP: A Workspace Delegation Protocol for Deep-Engagement Collaboration across Remote Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>.
The <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@awcp/mcp</span> package exposes seven MCP tools covering the full delegation lifecycle, including initiation, output monitoring, cancellation, snapshot management, and session recovery, enabling MCP-compatible agents such as Claude Desktop and Cline to manage delegations through standard tool calls.
A standalone Bun-based skill module provides equivalent functionality for chat-oriented platforms.</p>
</div>
